<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uqaylid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 990–<a href="/years/1096">1096</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Uqaylids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Uqaylid dynasty was an Arab Shia dynasty of the Banu Uqayl that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a> and much of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and the Jazira from about 990 to 1096. It rose as Buyid and Hamdanid power declined, and its emir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muslim-ibn-quraysh">Muslim ibn Quraysh</a> extended its rule to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a> in the 1080s. The dynasty was eclipsed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> at the end of the 11th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uqaylid-dynasty.jpg" alt="Uqaylid dynasty" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ali Zifan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uqaylid_dynasty_(greatest_extent).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
